cmd/launcher/main.go (~1656 lines) holds the MCP tool handlers, file tools, script tools, bridge preparation, lifecycle wiring, MCP config output and the hermes-setup sub-command. About 35 open cards point at it, and cards that edit it must run serially. Split it inside package main so later cards can run in parallel across disjoint files.

Proposed split (from the 2026-11-21 triage; adjust where call sites say otherwise):
- main.go: version, main, run, extractSubcommand, secs, boolVal, hasArg, hasPromptArg, allowWord, perm, strictWord
- tools.go: registerTools (incl. approve), serviceAction
- filetools.go: registerFileTools (resolve closure, read_file/list_dir/write_file/edit_file), requiredPathSchema, optionalPathSchema
- scripts.go: scriptPrefix, scriptExts, runtimeDir, scriptAction, sweepStaleScripts, isStaleScriptName, prepareRuntimes
- bridge.go: prepareMCPBridges, prepareNodeBridge, smokeTestMCP, waitForEndpoint
- lifecycle.go: makeAgentExitHandler, promptAgentExit, commandLoop, killCrashReporter, cleanRecovery
- mcpconfig.go: buildMCPServers, writeMCPConfigs, toVSCode
- helpers.go: warnIfMissing, fileExists, errResult, tailLines, getString, stringArg, getInt, firstString, firstMap
- hermes.go: hermesConfigMarker, runHermesSetup, resolveHermesConfigPath, loadHermesYAML, mergeHermesServer, writeYAMLAtomic

Placement to check by call site: generateBearerToken, localOverridePath and persistGeneratedToken are called from run() as well as from hermes-setup, so they do not belong in hermes.go alone.

Rules:
- Move declarations verbatim. No renames, no signature changes, no logic edits; run() stays one function in main.go.
- Folds in k83: move the orphaned commandLoop doc comment from above makeAgentExitHandler onto commandLoop.
- No build tags, go:embed or init() exist in the package; keep it that way.
- Done when: gofmt clean, go vet ./... clean, go test ./... green, make windows and make linux build; git diff shows moves only (plus the k83 comment). Verify that with a declaration inventory before/after (e.g. go doc -all / a grep of ^func, ^type, ^var, ^const), not by eye.

